  "description": "QIFLEZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C170 H160 O24 Sm10,C4 H8 O1. From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 4 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 4 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm5 (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm6 (Sm) has 2 O neighbors; Sm7 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm8 (Sm) has 4 O neighbors; Sm9 (Sm) has 5 O neighbors; Sm10 (Sm) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 17 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.532-4.420 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.14-142.21°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm10O4({C13H8}O)10(thf)10]·THF.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
